comments":3,"created_at":"2024-11-23T08:12:49Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T14:00:02Z","closed_at":"2024-11-23T13:59:57Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.22631 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6081) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-12900 (24 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing 'undo' on a new point in a curve2d corrupts the curve data and can cause the editor to crash.\nPossibly the same as ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/96636 ) but per the thread that one doesn't cause problems using Control+Z (only the history bar).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a new point on a path2d by clicking on it.  Attempt to remove this new point by pressing control+Z.  An error pops up.\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e146a08f-d0e3-414d-924c-3e86072d4aa9\n\n\nThe editor is now in a glitched state where the curve2d no longer responds properly.  No point in the curve can be edited, and the curve2d cannot be removed from the path2d.  In addition, continuing work with this corrupted curve can result in the editor crashing, though am not sure of exact trigger conditions.  Windows game bar does not record submenus, but clicking on the curve2d and selecting 'clear' fails to remove it from the path2d.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5284821-bbe3-4bb3-aa09-26ed8e35322b)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/081a80bb-33fc-42b3-ba1a-0b5f513eb60d\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nCan be done in a blank project by just adding a path2d and creating a curve.","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_